        {
          "title": "Verb + -ing after enjoy, stop, start",
          "rule": "Some verbs are always followed by another verb ending in \"-ing\" (a gerund): enjoy, stop, start, keep. \"Like\" and \"love\" are flexible — both forms are correct: I like cooking = I like to cook.",
          "examples": [
            "I enjoy walking in the park.",
            "I stopped smoking.",
            "I started studying English."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Verb + to + verb after want, need, have, plan, hope",
          "rule": "Other verbs are always followed by \"to\" + the base form of the next verb (an infinitive): want, need, have, plan, hope. Never add \"-ing\" after these.",
